**alinja** (Nov 16, 2023):
The original unsigned comparison had about a 30-second wraparound period at 125MHz. When mtime neared its maximum, "mtimecmp will wrap around and an interrupt is generated immediately." The signed comparison approach ensures interrupts trigger correctly across wraparound boundaries, though limiting advance scheduling to approximately 15 seconds.

